#### 5. Implementação em Java/C# assíncrono

O componente em Java/C# será responsável por armazenar os resultados no banco de dados. Utilizaremos assincronia para garantir que o armazenamento seja eficiente e não bloqueie o sistema.

##### Java

```java
import java.net.http.HttpClient;
import java.net.http.HttpRequest;
import java.net.http.HttpResponse;
import java.net.URI;
import java.net.http.HttpClient.Version;
import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;

public class StorageService {
	private static final HttpClient client = HttpClient.newHttpClient();

	public static CompletableFuture<Void> storeData(double mean, double[] anomalies) {
		String json = String.format("{\"mean\": %f, \"anomalies\": [%s]}", mean, String.join(", ", String.valueOf(anomalies)));
		HttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()
			.uri(URI.create("http://database:5432/store"))
			.header("Content-Type", "application/json")
			.POST(HttpRequest.BodyPublishers.ofString(json))
			.build();

		return client.sendAsync(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString())
			.thenApply(response -> {
				System.out.println(response.body());
				return null;
			});
	}
}
```

